{
 "$comment": [
  "Rear-camera geometry per phone, for biosphere.pano.devices. DATA, NOT CODE: adding",
  "a phone is one entry here and nothing else.",
  "",
  "video_equiv_mm is the 35mm-equivalent focal length of the 1x rear camera ON THE",
  "DIAGONAL CONVENTION (CIPA, 43.267 mm reference), for the frame the capture app",
  "actually records -- 1080x1440, which is the sensor's own 4:3 aspect, so no video",
  "crop applies. If the app ever records 16:9 these numbers need a crop factor of",
  "about 1.1. focal_px = video_equiv_mm * diagonal_px / 43.267.",
  "",
  "sigma_fraction is the honest one-sigma uncertainty, and the solve is bounded at two",
  "of them: 0.06 where the lens was measured on the device, 0.08 where a manufacturer",
  "published the figure, 0.12 where it is an estimate.",
  "",
  "aliases are exact navigator.userAgentData model strings, lower-cased. On Android",
  "that is ro.product.model -- the SKU, not the marketing name: a vivo Y22s reports",
  "V2206 and a Galaxy S23 reports SM-S911B. Apple reports nothing at all, which is",
  "what ios_fingerprints is for.",
  "",
  "Regenerate with scratchpad/merge_devices.py; hand edits are fine too."
 ],
